## Why This Question Matters

This question assesses your understanding of end-to-end data isolation, cross-region replication, retention governance, and PII redaction across a data lake, transformed layers, and BI dashboards—essential skills for building enterprise-compliant multi-tenant systems.

## Key Concepts to Demonstrate

- Multi-tenant data isolation across raw and transformed layers
- Per-tenant retention and purge workflows with full auditability
- Cross-region replication latency and consistency guarantees
- PII redaction verification across caches and dashboards
- Seed data design and deterministic testing signals

## Code Example

```javascript
// Seed tenants for deterministic E2E tests
const tenants = [
  { id: 't1', name: 'Acme Corp', region: 'us-east-1' },
  { id: 't2', name: 'Globex', region: 'eu-west-1' }
];

// Simulate event streams from mobile and web
async function seedEventStream(tenant, source) {
  const events = generateEvents(tenant.id, source, 1000);
  await publishToIngestTopic(tenant.region, events);
}

// Verify isolation: ensure t1 cannot access t2 data
async function verifyIsolation() {
  const t1Raw = await queryRawLake('t1');
  const t2Raw = await queryRawLake('t2');
  expect(t1Raw).not.toContainTenantData('t2');
  expect(t2Raw).not.toContainTenantData('t1');
}

// Verify PII redaction in transformed views
async function verifyRedaction() {
  const transformed = await queryTransformedView('t1');
  expect(transformed).toHaveRedacted('email');
  expect(transformed).toHaveRedacted('phone');
}
```

## Verification Matrix

| Layer | Isolation | Redaction | Retention |
|-------|-----------|-----------|------------|
| Raw Lake | ✓ | N/A | ✓ |
| Transformed | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Cache | ✓ | ✓ | N/A |
| BI Dashboard | ✓ | ✓ | N/A |

## Essential Metrics

- **Isolation violations**: Zero cross-tenant data leaks
- **Redaction coverage**: 100% of defined PII fields
- **Replication lag**: < 5s for sync, < 60s for async regions
- **Retention accuracy**: Auto-purge at tenant-specified TTL
- **Query latency**: P95 < 500ms for dashboard queries

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests your ability to design end-to-end tests for offline-first collaborative applications—a common pattern in modern productivity tools. It evaluates understanding of multi-client synchronization, conflict resolution strategies, and proper test isolation.

## Key Concepts
- **Offline-first syncing and eventual consistency**: Understanding how data propagates when clients reconnect
- **Conflict resolution strategies**: CRDT (Conflict-free Replicated Data Types) ensures deterministic merging; last-writer-wins uses timestamps
- **Multi-client test isolation**: Using separate browser contexts to simulate concurrent users
- **Network simulation**: Leveraging tools like Playwright's network throttling to emulate offline/online transitions
- **Per-note permissions and presence**: Validating access control and real-time user indicators

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright setup with two isolated contexts
const { chromium } = require('playwright');

const browser = await chromium.launch();
const context1 = await browser.newContext();
const context2 = await browser.newContext();

const user1 = await context1.newPage();
const user2 = await context2.newPage();

// Seed shared note
const noteId = await createSharedNote(user1, 'Test Note');
await user2.goto(`/notes/${noteId}`);

// Take user1 offline
await context1.setOffline(true);

// User1 edits offline
await user1.fill('.editor', 'User1 offline edit');

// User2 edits online
await user2.fill('.editor', 'User2 online edit');

// Restore connectivity
await context1.setOffline(false);

// Verify sync and conflict resolution
const finalContent = await user1.textContent('.editor');
console.log('Final content:', finalContent);
```

